<!--Post: 2170--><!--Time: 1103359470-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2170"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Alobster7<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Alobster7<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, December 18, 2004 - 12:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Looks like even if BTK is captured &#40;and lives in Kansas&#41; he can not get the death penalty - <BR> <BR><a href="http://news.yahoo.com/news?tmpl=story&amp;u=/nm/20041217/us_nm/executions_kansas_dc_2" target=_top>http://news.yahoo.com/news?tmpl=story&amp;u=/nm/200412 17/us_nm/executions_kansas_dc_2</a> <BR> <BR> <BR>YUK!!! <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2170-->
<!--Post: 2286--><!--Time: 1103497681-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2286"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hackenmaster@cox.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 19, 2004 - 3:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->kansas does have the death penalty, but due to Nola Foulston coming up with the hard 40 sentence is rarely &#40;except in BTK&#39;s case&#41; used.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2286-->
<!--Post: 3156--><!--Time: 1104528882-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3156"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 1:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK would be prosecuted and sentenced under the law in effect at the time, which included the death penalty.  The old Kansas capital punishment laws were never ruled unconstitutional.  After the U.S. Supreme Court decided Furman v. Georgia, Kansas’s prosecutors assumed the statute was defective and it wasn’t used again.  That assumption was never tested, and the death penalty remained the law until it was replaced by the current law, which was ruled unconstitutional.    It is quite possible to prosecute BTK and sentence him to death under the previous statutes.  The death sentence would almost certainly be reversed on appeal, but you never know until you try.   <BR> <BR>Besides, there was no automatic review of a death sentence under former law.  If BTK didn’t appeal his conviction, he would be hung.  That might appeal to him. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3156-->
<!--Post: 3278--><!--Time: 1104727224-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3278"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 02, 2005 - 8:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK being hung would certainly appeal to him, as I&#39;m sure he isn&#39;t. <BR> <BR>BTK being hanged would certainly appeal to me. ;&#41; <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3278-->
